                "dsDescriptionValue": {
                  "typeName": "dsDescriptionValue",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "World Input-Output Tables and underlying data, covering 43 countries, and a model for the rest of the world for the period 2000-2014. Data for 56 sectors are classified according to the International Standard Industrial Classification revision 4 (ISIC Rev. 4). The tables adhere to the 2008 version of the SNA. Additionally underlying supply and use tables (SUT) are available, as well as Socio Economic Accounts (SEA). <a href=\"https://www.rug.nl/ggdc/valuechain/new-wiod/wiod-2016-release\">Associated Website</a><br><br>\nWhen using this database, a reference should be made to the following paper:\nTimmer, M. P., Dietzenbacher, E., Los, B., Stehrer, R. and de Vries, G. J. (2015),\n<a href=\"http://dx.doi.org/10.1111/roie.12178\">\"An Illustrated User Guide to the World Input–Output Database: the Case of Global Automotive Production\"</a>,\nReview of International Economics., 23: 575–605<br>"
